.TH ZCALLD 1 "November 2026" "zcalld" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zcalld \- compact native AI gateway with optional plugins
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zcalld
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zcalld
serves a local AI gateway on Linux, macOS and Windows.
The zcall library handles model protocols. System libcurl provides HTTP and TLS
transport. Optional native plugins are loaded through zplugin and its shared
zsys platform loader.
.PP
Linux and macOS can expose both a private Unix socket and a compatible TCP
listener. Local management clients prefer the configured Unix socket.
The optional zcall-gui application is a separate process and package.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create a starter configuration without replacing an existing file.
.TP
.B serve
Run the gateway in the foreground. Under systemd, report readiness after startup.
.TP
.B check
Validate configuration and load configured native plugins without asking a
remote model to generate a response.
.TP
.BR health " | " status
Inspect the live local gateway or the installed service and configuration.
.TP
.B models
Print public model routes and retained capability metadata.
.TP
.B env
Print client environment settings. An optional argument selects
.BR openai ,
.BR anthropic ,
or
.BR gemini .
.TP
.B providers
List, add, edit or remove provider configuration; inspect models or test a
provider. Plugin account tests identify when only local configuration was
validated. They do not report an unperformed remote request as successful.
.TP
.BR routes " | " groups
List, set or remove model routes and model groups.
.TP
.B agents
Discover supported installed agents, inspect the adapter catalog, apply gateway
configuration or revert an owned change.
.TP
.B privacy
Show saved privacy settings or select
.BR off ,
.BR secrets ,
or
.BR personal .
First activation can require starting or restarting the daemon to load its
plugin binding. Saved settings and verified runtime state are reported separately.
.TP
.B plugins
Inspect native or community plugins; install, enable, disable, remove, update
or configure community packages through the optional compatibility helper.
Newly installed community packages remain disabled until explicitly enabled.
.TP
.B accounts
List, import, select, enable, disable or remove provider accounts, or inspect
session metadata through the compatibility helper.
.TP
.B profiles
List, save or select configuration profiles.
.TP
.B library
Manage MCP servers, instruction sets and skill directories. Top-level operations
include list, import, export, targets, apply and revert. The
.BR mcp ,
.B instructions
and
.B skills
subcommands provide their own configuration operations. Use
.B \-\-agent
to select a target and
.B \-\-dry-run
to inspect an application plan. Owned changes can be reverted; unrelated
configuration and independently edited files are preserved.
.TP
.B usage
Summarize or export the local usage ledger, including imported Magpie rows.
.TP
.B migrate
Inspect or import Magpie configuration with
.BR "migrate magpie" .
The default operation is a preview. Use
.B \-\-apply
to create a private copy in a fresh destination.
Importing configuration does not stop Magpie or take over its port.
.TP
.B service
Start, stop, restart, enable, disable or inspect the platform service.
On Linux, the default is the current user's systemd unit;
.B \-\-system
selects the system unit.
.TP
.B update
Check for or apply an official update. Package-managed installations must use
their package manager; the portable updater does not overwrite package-owned
binaries.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-c, \-\-config " path
Use the specified configuration file, overriding
.B ZCALLD_CONFIG
and the platform default.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Request machine-readable output. Management commands already use JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-api-key-stdin
Read a provider credential from standard input for supported provider operations.
Do not put credentials in shell arguments or history.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the command overview.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/zcalld/config.conf
Default Linux user configuration when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
.TP
.B ~/.config/zcalld/credentials
Private provider credentials next to the user configuration.
The file uses literal NAME=value entries without shell expansion and must have
mode 0600.
.TP
.B /etc/zcalld/config.conf
Packaged system-configuration template. Package upgrades preserve local changes.
.TP
.B /var/lib/zcalld/config.conf
Active configuration for the packaged system service.
.TP
.B /var/lib/zcalld/credentials
Optional private credentials next to the system service configuration.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/zcalld/plugins/
Packaged optional native plugins. A plugin is loaded only when configured.
.TP
.B /usr/libexec/zcalld/
Optional compatibility executables for community accounts and privacy processing.
.SH SERVICE
Use one service scope for a given listening address and port.
The user unit reads the user's configuration and is suitable for desktop agents.
.PP
.B systemctl --user enable --now zcalld.service
.PP
The system unit runs as the static unprivileged zcalld user and reads
/var/lib/zcalld/config.conf. Its state directory must contain a reviewed,
service-owned configuration before starting. It deliberately cannot read a
desktop user's home directory. Use
.B sudo systemctl enable --now zcalld.service
only after preparing that state.
.PP
Both units allow the main process to drain compatibility workers during shutdown.
The Magpie cutover utility creates an additional reversible user-service
override and an independent private recovery script.
.SH CONFIGURATION DEFAULTS
Linux uses $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/zcalld or $HOME/.config/zcalld.
macOS uses $HOME/Library/Application Support/zcalld.
Windows uses %APPDATA%/zcalld.
The configuration file is named config.conf.
.SH SECURITY
Keep caller authentication separate from provider credentials.
Unix sockets use private ownership and permissions.
Native plugins are trusted code and execute with the service's privileges.
Install only reviewed community packages and native libraries.
Migration backups and recovery journals may contain credentials and must remain
private.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
.PP
Project and detailed configuration documentation:
https://github.com/LIghtJUNction/zcalld
